            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for a fixed term, then the Gujarati for to allot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: દેવાળું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દેવાળું — devāḷũ — \"bankruptcy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ધંધામાં ખોટ ગઈ અને વેપારીનું દેવાળું નીકળ્યું. dhandhāmā̃ khoṭ gaī ane vepārīnũ devāḷũ nīkaḷyũ. The business made a loss and the merchant went bankrupt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દેવાળું (devāḷũ) CDIAL lists Hindi diwālā and Punjabi davālā, \"bankruptcy\", under Sanskrit dīpāvali, \"a row of lamps\" (CDIAL 6358), the word behind દિવાળી; it gives no Gujarati form for દેવાળું, and how lamps came to mean ruin is not settled, so the link is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
